## Objective
Fix the exact installed `0.6.3-dev.20260831143001.1` continuity deadlock where a confirmed `active_wake` can remain `ACTIVE` indefinitely while the supervisor tab is already terminal/IDLE, blocking every queued successor wake.

## Live evidence
Supabase showed the installed Browser on exact release source `e0a44cddd5cc526bb2c1a856c871417ceddfa78b` with keepalive `1.3.0`, state `ACTIVE`, an old confirmed active wake, terminal/IDLE supervisor state, a rebound supervisor tab after `target closed while handling command`, and queued successor wakes that could not run.

## Changes
- add fail-closed active-wake terminal retirement proof;
- preserve normal generation→terminal retirement;
- allow already-IDLE retirement only for restored durable active requests or exact current-tab rebind after grace;
- require exact wake id, current keepalive tab and generation epoch;
- explicitly reject the just-sent IDLE race;
- clear via `markCycleComplete()` without sending/retrying an effect;
- allow the same lifecycle cycle to issue the next queued successor;
- add pure and lifecycle regressions reproducing the live failure.

No main merge, production promotion, arbitrary eval, blind retry, second scheduler or authority weakening.

## Objective
Fix the actual installed DevOS task-dispatch path on the current Browser release lineage, without regressing elastic fleet, supervisor mesh, effect binding, resilience, or self-update work.

## Exact installed substrate
Current installed release `v0.6.3-dev.20260831143001.1` targets Git SHA `e0a44cddd5cc526bb2c1a856c871417ceddfa78b`, which is the head of `work/devos-elastic-fleet-bootstrap-v1`. This PR is based directly on that exact branch.

## Root cause
`DevOsNativeTaskCycle.#dispatchLease()` still used `CAPTURE -> SEMANTIC_TYPE(submit_after_type=true/Enter) -> CAPTURE`. Live evidence repeatedly produced `AMBIGUOUS_AFTER_ENTER` on background/zero-viewport worker tabs. The old proof also accepted any post-send conversation URL, allowing an existing `/c/...` URL to falsely prove a no-op effect.

## Changes
- add a pure foreground/nonzero-viewport/unique-composer/unique-Send readiness contract;
- save the pre-dispatch selected tab and foreground the exact worker via typed `SELECT_TAB`;
- read back selected-tab identity and exact live fleet task/agent/tab/target/generation binding;
- capture and require a renderable viewport before typing;
- type prompt with `submit_after_type=false`;
- re-read selected tab and exact lease binding after typing;
- recapture and revalidate viewport/composer/Send before the only Send effect;
- issue exactly one typed `TYPED_CLICK` for Send;
- prove transport only from STOP or a root-to-conversation transition; an already-existing conversation URL alone is never proof;
- report ambiguous on type/click/readiness loss and never retry the effect;
- restore the prior tab only if the worker tab is still selected, so a user tab change is never overwritten;
- preserve the existing single DB-native scheduler and exact fleet proof-before-mark-running wrapper.

## Tests
Regression coverage includes foreground selection, two-phase type/click order, prior-tab restoration, zero viewport pre-effect rejection, existing-conversation no-op ambiguity, one-click-only semantics, and user tab override preservation.

No main merge, no production promotion, no live Browser retry, no arbitrary eval, no second scheduler. Requires exact Browser Shell and physical Self Update E2E before any release consideration.

## Objective
Wire the physically motivated two-phase fleet task dispatcher behind the trusted C5 Browser composition without exposing the raw FleetProvisioner, raw dispatcher, or proof-input surface.

## Exact parent
Stacked on PR #136 exact GREEN head `f1385df0ac472fe1812e306b85684daaf3d3bbd6`.

## Additional P0 proof repair
Before wiring, this child fixes a proof bug in the parent dispatcher: an already-existing `/c/...` URL is no longer sufficient to prove a send effect. Post-click success now requires either exactly one STOP control or an observed root→conversation transition. An existing conversation with no STOP remains `AMBIGUOUS_AFTER_CLICK`, with no automatic retry or promotion.

## Runtime composition slice
- `createFleetBrowserComposition()` now owns the two-phase dispatcher behind a narrow `dispatchTask(payload)` method;
- Browser-main-local dependencies supply selection, selected-tab readback, WebContents lookup, semantic capture and typed semantic effects;
- exact agent/tab/target/generation validation remains inside the dispatcher;
- prompt typing is separate from the one Send click;
- raw dispatcher/provisioner/proof inputs remain unexposed;
- renderer and worker Browser authority remain false;
- no second scheduler is introduced.

## Evidence tests
- exact foreground two-phase composition dispatch promotes only after trusted post-readback;
- existing conversation no-op click remains ambiguous and cannot promote;
- no arbitrary eval/execution surface is exposed.

No live Browser retry, no production DDL, no main/integration merge, no release promotion. Exact Browser Shell + Self Update E2E are required before any further runtime rejoin.

## Objective
Replace the geometry-independent Enter-based fleet submit path with an explicitly foreground, two-phase, evidence-gated send contract.

## Exact parent
Parent PR #134 head `6cc5ca95ae9219b5de296b93380360b10b540fe7` adds the pure foreground/nonzero-viewport readiness contract.

## Changes
- trusted caller must provide Browser-main-local `selectTab` and `getSelectedTabId` dependencies;
- exact WebContents target incarnation is checked before selection and again after selection;
- foreground selection must be positively read back;
- pre-type readiness requires exact tab/target, nonzero viewport, unique composer and unique Send;
- prompt insertion uses `SEMANTIC_TYPE` with `submit_after_type=false`;
- foreground/target/viewport/controls are revalidated after typing and before Send;
- Send is one separately fenced `TYPED_CLICK` effect;
- click return itself does not prove delivery; only canonical conversation URL / STOP post-readback can promote transport;
- missing post-send proof becomes `AMBIGUOUS_AFTER_CLICK`, automatic retry false;
- v3 receipt now truthfully records selected-tab mutation and viewport/mouse geometry requirements;
- adversarial tests cover zero viewport, selection failure, pre/post-selection target replacement, readiness loss after typing, foreground loss after typing, and ambiguous click with no duplicate click.

No live Browser retry, no runtime composition wiring, no second scheduler, no arbitrary eval, no main merge, no production promotion. Runtime wiring is a separately evidence-gated child.

## Objective
Stack a research-derived Git worktree hardening slice on the DBR1 Workspace Manager core.

## Evidence
Current Git documentation recommends `git worktree list --porcelain -z` as stable machine-readable output and supports `git worktree add --lock --reason` to lock the worktree at creation without a race. Linked worktrees have private Git metadata plus a shared common Git directory, so DBR1 must verify actual Git inventory rather than infer ownership from paths alone.

## Changes
- atomically plans locked worktree creation using fixed argv and exact base;
- adds read-only `git worktree list --porcelain -z` inventory plan;
- parses the stable porcelain format;
- proves exact managed path, branch ref, HEAD and locked/non-prunable state;
- rejects missing/ambiguous path, unlocked, prunable, detached, wrong-head and wrong-branch inventory;
- cleanup preserves the DBR1 reference/dirty/ambiguity fences and models unlock+remove as one same-executor-lease sequence;
- no force remove/reset/branch deletion.

No scheduler, arbitrary eval, main merge, production DDL, Browser live actuation or release promotion.

## Objective
Eliminate the observed DBR1 fleet transport ambiguity caused by sending from background/zero-viewport ChatGPT worker views.

## Evidence
Live supervisor cycles observed `SEMANTIC_TYPE submit_after_type` ending `AMBIGUOUS_AFTER_ENTER` while read-only capture showed a zero-size background viewport and the Send control still present. Current CDP mouse coordinates are viewport-relative; this slice converts that condition into a deterministic pre-effect reject.

## Changes
- adds pure `evaluateFleetSubmitReadiness()`;
- requires exact expected/observed/selected tab identity;
- requires exact target incarnation;
- rejects already-generating workers;
- requires nonzero renderable viewport;
- requires unique composer and unique Send control;
- returns only `TYPE_WITHOUT_SUBMIT_THEN_TYPED_CLICK_SEND` readiness;
- automatic retry, page authority and authority effect remain false;
- adversarial tests cover background tab, zero viewport, stale target, active generation and ambiguous controls.

This is a readiness contract only; runtime wiring remains a separately evidence-gated child. No live Browser retry, no scheduler, no arbitrary eval, no main merge or production promotion.

## Objective
Repair the fleet background-submit reliability gap observed during supervisor wake cycle 11 without adding SELECT_TAB, mouse geometry, a second scheduler, or any retry-after-ambiguity path.

## Live failure evidence
A leased planner worker received `SEMANTIC_TYPE submit_after_type=true`; the existing implementation found exactly one semantic Send control but sent Enter while focus remained on the composer. Live receipt returned `AMBIGUOUS_AFTER_ENTER`; readback proved no effect. Durable worker leases subsequently began expiring as `LEASE_EXPIRED_EFFECT_UNKNOWN`.

## Smallest fix
- preserve exact ChatGPT composer validation and unique semantic Send requirement;
- after text insertion, focus the exact SEND backend node with `DOM.focus`;
- only then dispatch one Enter activation;
- keep the existing bounded STOP/new-conversation readback;
- add `submit_method=EXACT_SEND_FOCUSED_ENTER` to evidence;
- preserve `automatic_retry_allowed=false` and existing ambiguous effect semantics for compatibility;
- no viewport, box-model, mouse geometry, selected-tab mutation or arbitrary page JS/eval.

## Tests
Updated `fleet-background-submit.test.mjs` proves:
- composer then exact Send focus ordering;
- Enter occurs only after Send focus;
- no DOM box model / mouse / layout metrics;
- missing Send fails before submit;
- ambiguous activation is single-shot with no retry.

No main merge, no production promotion, no live Browser actuation is performed by this PR.

## Objective
Implement the smallest safe DBR1 Workspace Manager core on exact C5 Browser fleet composition head `ebb5963a376fa5d8bb53a345457d298594d7b590`.

Planner evidence: `work/devbrowser-workspace-plan-v1` checkpoint `cdb58487cab2a1dbcdc72aa0c8013d39726dad2d`.

## Changes
- exact `coordination_workspace + task + claim + base + branch + agent + tab + target + agent_generation + lease_generation` validation;
- manager-derived worktree path under a trusted root; caller/page/model cannot supply the physical worktree path;
- fixed `git` executable + argv materialization/removal plans with `shell=false`;
- exact-base `git worktree add -b <branch> <managed-path> <base_sha>` plan;
- branch-preexists fails closed pending separately proven rehydration support;
- materialization readback only promotes to READY when exact initial HEAD and managed realpath match;
- ambiguous effect, initial-HEAD drift, realpath drift and explicit freeze become FROZEN with `automatic_retry_allowed=false`;
- cleanup rejects active references, dirty state, branch ambiguity, or non-READY state; branch deletion is intentionally excluded;
- adversarial tests cover advisory claims, malformed identity, path traversal, ambiguity, head/path drift and cleanup fences.

## Authority model
This slice is branch-local only and does not lease tasks, create a second scheduler, execute arbitrary commands, grant page/model/worker authority, touch main, mutate production, or promote a release.

## Worker-loss context
The current supervisor cycle observed fleet task transport leases expiring into `LEASE_EXPIRED_EFFECT_UNKNOWN` because background ChatGPT dispatch remains unreliable. This PR does not retry those ambiguous effects; it advances DBR1 through trusted GitHub evidence while transport recovery remains separately fenced.

