Chromium-style successor qualification stacked on durable transaction journal.

A target boot stays SUCCESSOR_BOOTED until it proves:
- exact target version already bound by handoff;
- primary single-instance lock still held;
- minimum stable process uptime;
- persistent userData available;
- self-update session continuity capsule has been successfully consumed/cleared.

Only then transaction becomes QUALIFIED and clears swapping. Network/Supabase availability is intentionally not a hard qualification gate, so offline startup cannot quarantine a valid local install.

No release/main promotion.

Stacked on the sentinel-safe P0 repair. Adds a durable update transaction journal with atomic+fsync writes and explicit PREPARED / INSTALLING / SUCCESSOR_BOOTED / QUALIFIED / AMBIGUOUS_INSTALL / QUARANTINED / SUPERSEDED states.

Key invariants:
- `swapping` is durable while activation is incomplete;
- automatic retry is false for every in-flight/ambiguous transaction;
- exact source/target/version binding;
- invalid backward transitions are rejected;
- successor must match the exact target before qualification;
- handoff/startup paths persist ambiguity and boot evidence.

No main/release promotion.

Stacked on PR #92 (`work/browser-control-runtime-v1`). This closes the remaining self-update starvation mode and changes restart semantics per the Browser requirement: active ChatGPT/model generation is continuity state, not a restart blocker.

Implemented:
- removes `lifecycle.isQuiescent()` from the self-update restart gate;
- allows updater handoff while ChatGPT tabs are GENERATING, streaming, or while durable supervisor wake backlog exists;
- still blocks installer handoff while a local verified-download transaction is active and while NativeSupervisorClient is executing a typed command;
- adds an atomic `metaengine.self-update-session-continuity.v1` capsule before installer launch;
- capsule stores only HTTPS tab topology, selected tab, generation classification and sanitized lifecycle metadata; it explicitly stores no chat text, tab titles, prompt bodies or credentials;
- successor restores missing URLs and selected tab through existing typed `NEW_TAB` / `SELECT_TAB` actions before lifecycle startup;
- prior GENERATING chats are reconciled after restore without blind prompt replay: existing STOP means generation already continued; exact CONTINUE is clicked once with readback; unknown/capture-failed state causes no retry and leaves durable continuity evidence;
- restore is exact-target-version bound, URL-deduplicated and fail-closed on partial/unresolved restore; the capsule remains durable until a complete restore;
- session login/cookies remain in the existing persistent Electron partition;
- tests cover active-generation restart allowance, real VerifiedDownloadManager shape, privacy, atomic persistence, exact target-version restore, generating-chat reconciliation and wiring order.

This PR does not expose arbitrary eval/raw CDP/shell authority and does not merge main or change production authority. Full Browser Shell + physical N→N+1 evidence is required before publishing a dev successor and bootstrapping installed 77.1.

Stacked on PR #93. Adds a branch-local, append-only Supabase command contract for the new Browser Control Plane actions without switching live Edge/RPC authority.

Adds:
- command action constraint support for CONTROL_CAPABILITIES, KEY_PRESS and SET_ZOOM;
- issue_native_v2 with strict payload validation: capability discovery requires {}, KEY_PRESS only permits allowlisted keys/modifiers and optional exact tab_id, SET_ZOOM requires numeric factor 0.5–3.0 and rejects extra payload fields;
- sequential JSON type validation before array/cast operations so malformed payloads fail with typed validation errors rather than incidental PostgreSQL errors;
- lease_v4 action budget: capability discovery and other read-only diagnostics cost 0 and are available in MONITOR; KEY_PRESS/SET_ZOOM cost 1 and remain CONTROL-only;
- complete_v6 derives authority_effect from the action, marking KEY_PRESS/SET_ZOOM mutating while CONTROL_CAPABILITIES stays read-only;
- service_role-only execute grants for the new RPCs;
